  "query_preview": "(Today through Saturday)...\nIssued at 314 AM EDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nCooler and drier conditions will start off the new week behind the \npassage of a cold front and a Canadian airmass at the lower levels \nsagging into the Great Lakes region. Highs the next couple of days \nwill stay in the 80s with lows dropping into the 60s and even 50s in \nsome areas. \n\nThis return to near normal temperatures will only be short lived as \nupper ridging returns, bringing the heat back with it. Luckily this \ntime the heat will be brief as the upper pattern is more progressive \nthan was seen last week, allowing broad upper troughing to arrive \nmid to late week. A shortwave with this trough will bring with it \nanother surface cold front and potentially a round of showers and \nstorms. Confidence is growing in this round of rain mid to late week \nas models start to have better agreement on the timing of the wave. \nTemperatures are again expected to drop back to near normal again \nbehind the wave and largely persist into the weekend. Models are \nhinting at another potential chance of storms late next weekend.",
